Subject: [PATCH 3/6] Bluetooth: handle LHDC V3 source and sink in exhaustive
 codec switches

The Android 17 LHDC migration added native V3 source/sink indexes but missed CodecNameStr, causing libbtif btif_av.cc to fail with -Werror=switch. Add their explicit names. Mark the OEM-dependent V3 codecs outside the portable stack fixture supported set so its exhaustive switch also remains valid. Scanned Bluetooth C/C++ switches for codec-index cases without defaults. The original failed ARM64/APEX36 btif_av.o compiler invocation now exits 0 with the existing warning policy. Whitespace passed. Unified images and runtime audio acceptance remain pending.

