From bba5e5061ec6fa3147db506e3b863a2633e811e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tunkoal <tunkoal@163.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:37:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] Bluetooth: isolate OEM V3 quote headers from the upstream
 V5 API

The shared stack include_dirs placed external/liblhdc before the Rust V5 exported headers, selecting old lhdcv5BT.h/lhdcv5_api.h and failing the V5 encoder types. Restrict OEM paths to -iquote and use explicit quote includes at the two V3 OEM API sites, for both production and portable-test modules. The unmodified upstream V5 angle include resolves through its existing Rust library dependency. Eight ARM64/APEX36 C++ objects compiled with the existing warning policy. Dependency files prove V3 uses OEM headers and V5 uses only upstream API headers. Whitespace passed. Soong regeneration, full link, IMG and device audio validation pending.

